## Invocation

Run the verb with the user's arguments and surface its stdout/stderr to the user:

```bash
nix run .#pyfars -- {{ name }} $ARGUMENTS
```

This invocation routes through the substrate's runtime — if the `{{ name }}` verb mutates substrate state or asserts an observation, it will append a bilattice-valued `Witness` to `.pyfars/event-log/<date>.jsonl` on its own channel. The plugin is pure envelope; the witness chain is the same one a direct `pyfars {{ name }}` invocation would produce.
